  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10b-2002-p13.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Grouping and factoring, \\[ \\begin{aligned} &8xy - 12y + 2x - 3 \\\\ &= 4y(2x - 3) + (2x - 3) \\\\ &= (4y + 1)(2x - 3). \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nFor this to equal \\(0\\) for all \\(y,\\) the factor that depends on \\(y\\) cannot be forced to zero, so we need \\(2x - 3 = 0,\\) giving \\(x = \\dfrac32.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Group terms to factor the left side",
        "\\(8xy - 12y + 2x - 3\\) \\(= (4y + 1)(2x - 3)\\); it must vanish for every \\(y\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
